  "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $1:4$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the number of cups of water ($1$), and the denominator represents the number of seeds ($4$).\n\nWe can make a numerator of $7$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $7$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1\\times 7}{4\\times 7} & =\\frac{7}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| Water (cups) | Seeds |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ |\n| $7$ | $28$ |\n| $12$ | $48$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, Gerry can plant $28$ seeds with $7$ cups of water.",
